betelgeuz.profiles.markdownDescription:
Named SSH profiles shared by every workspace. Each entry describes one board: `host`, `port`, `username`, `credentialRef`, and the identity pins.

Example:
```json
{
  "my-board": {
    "host": "192.168.7.1",
    "username": "root",
    "credentialRef": "board-key",
    "hostKey": "SHA256:..."
  }
}
```

Store passwords, private keys, and passphrases through Betelgeuz commands so they stay in VS Code SecretStorage — never in this setting.
